{title: O Holy Night}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

[C]O holy night! the [F]stars are brightly [C]shining,
It is the night of the [G7]dear Savior's [C]birth.
Long lay the world in [F]sin and error [C]pin[C7]ing,
Till He ap[Em]peared and the [B7]soul felt its [Em]worth.
A [G7]thrill of hope, the [C]weary world rejoices,
For [G7]yonder breaks a [C]new and glorious morn.

[Am]Fall on your [Em]knees! Oh, [Dm]hear the angel [Am]voices!
O [C]night [G7]di[C]vine! [F]O [C]night [G7]when Christ was [C]born!
O [G7]night di[C]vine! [Dm]O [C]night, [G7]O night di[C]vine!

[C]Led by the light of [F]faith serenely [C]beaming,
With glowing hearts by his [G7]cradle we [C]stand.
So, led by light of [F]a star sweetly [C]gleam[C7]ing,
Here came the [Em]wise men from [B7]the Orient [Em]land.
The [G7]King of kings lay [C]thus in lowly manger,
In [G7]all our trials [C]born to be our friend.

[Am]He knows our [Em]need, to [Dm]our weakness no [Am]stranger.
Be[C]hold [G7]your [C]King, [F]be[C]fore [G7]him lowly [C]bend!
Be[G7]hold your [C]King, [Dm]your [C]King, [G7]before him [C]bend!

[C]Truly he taught us [F]to love one an[C]other;
His law is love and his [G7]gospel is [C]peace.
Chains shall he break, for [F]the slave is our [C]broth[C7]er,
And in his [Em]name all op[B7]pression shall [Em]cease.
Sweet [G7]hymns of joy in [C]grateful chorus raise we;
Let [G7]all within us [C]praise his holy name.

[Am]Christ is the [Em]Lord! Then [Dm]ever, ever [Am]praise we,
His [C]power [G7]and [C]glo[F]ry [C]ev[G7]ermore pro[C]claim!
His [G7]power and [C]glo[Dm]ry [C]ev[G7]ermore pro[C]claim!
